   - For example, if \( s = 1 \), the rate of formation of the RR dimer is equal to the rate of formation of the meso dimer, and no enhancement of the initial enantiomeric excess is observed.
   - If \( s > 1 \), the rate of formation of the RR dimer is faster than the rate of formation of the meso dimer, leading to an increase in the enantiomeric excess of the RR enantiomer.

