     \]
   - The sodium ion (Na⁺) is a spectator ion, meaning it does not participate in the reaction. Therefore, the net ionic equation is:
     \[
     \text{C}_7\text{H}_6\text{O}_2 (s) + \text{OH}^- (aq) \rightarrow \text{C}_7\text{H}_5\text{O}_2^- (aq) + \text{H}_2\text{O} (l)
     \]

**Explanation**:
- Benzoic acid (C₇H₆O₂) is a weak acid, so it don't fully dissociate in water.
