a) **Practical structure**  
For a system with \( n \) components in a single-dimensional order, the system's reliability is the product of the individual probabilities of each component:  
\[
R_S(t) = \prod_{i=1}^{n} R_i(t) = R_1(t) \times R_2(t) \times \cdots \times R_n(t)
\]  
