- \( z_1 = +2 \) (for Ca²⁺)
- \( z_2 = -1 \) (for Cl⁻)
- The Boltzmann constant \( k = 8.854 \times 10^{-12} \, \text{F m}^{-1} \)
- The given constant \( 2.21 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{J nm} \) is a simplified form of the Born-Lander constant, which includes Coulomb's constant and the electrostatic force.

Using the given constant:
\[
\text{Lattice energy} = 2.21 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{J nm} \times 0.231 \, \text{nm}
\]
