2 CO(g) + O2(g) → 2 CO2(g)

Now, we can find the standard enthalpy change (ΔH°) for the reaction using the standard enthalpies of formation (ΔHf°) of the reactants and products. The standard enthalpy of formation is the change in enthalpy when one mole of a compound is formed from its elements in their standard states.

