- \( \mu_0 \) is the permeability of free air (\( 4.5 \times 10^{-7} \, \text{T m A}^{-1} \))
- \( N \) is the number of turns in the coil
- \( I \) is the current (in Amperes)
- \( r \) is the radius of the coil (in meters)

Substituting the given values:
- \( N = 100 \)
- \( I = 1 \, \text{A} \)
- \( r = 0.2 \, \text{m} \)

\[
B = \frac{(4.5 \times 10^{-7} \, \text{T m A}^{-1}) \times 100 \times 1 \, \text{A}}{2 \times 0.2 \, \text{m}}
\]

\[
B = \frac{4.5 \times 10^{-5} \, \text{T m}}{0.4 \, \text{m}}
\]

\[
B = 1.125 \times 10^{-4} \, \text{T}
\]

