   - **Solid Solution Strengthening:** Copper atoms, being larger than aluminum atoms, will solvens in the aluminum lattice, creating defects (defortract defects). These defects distort the lattice and hinder the movement of dislocations, which are necessary for deformation. As dislocations must overcome these defects to move, more stress is required to cause deformation, leading to a higher yield strength.
